# Document toolbar actions (Print / Download)

On small screens, Print, Download PDF, and similar document/tool actions in page headings must be **icon-only**. Desktop keeps icon + short label.

## Markup

Wrap the action group in `doc-actions` (add page-specific class only if needed):

```tsx
<div className="button-row no-print doc-actions">
  <button
    type="button"
    className="button secondary"
    aria-label="Print"
    title="Print"
  >
    <Printer size={16} aria-hidden="true" />
    <span className="button-label">Print</span>
  </button>
  <button
    type="button"
    className="button"
    aria-label="Download PDF"
    title="Download PDF"
  >
    <Download size={16} aria-hidden="true" />
    <span className="button-label">PDF</span>
  </button>
</div>
```

## Required

- Put visible text in `<span className="button-label">…</span>` so CSS can hide it ≤680px.
- Always set `aria-label` and `title` (tooltips matter when labels hide).
- Mark decorative icons `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Prefer short labels on desktop (`Print`, `PDF`) not long phrases in tight headers.

## Do not

- Put Print/Download label text as a bare text node next to the icon (mobile cannot hide it cleanly).
- Use icon-only on desktop for these primary doc actions unless the control is already a row `icon-button` (e.g. document library tables).

## CSS

Shared rules live in `apps/web/app/globals.css` under `.doc-actions` (and aliases `.boarding-doc-actions`, `.booking-print-actions`, `.pickup-print-actions`). Reuse those; do not invent per-page mobile hide hacks.
